WEBVTT

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:06.610
Rook!

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:27.000
Kaito's been...

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.810
Yes, Mr. President.

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:29.890
<i>How's his condition?</i>

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:31.460
He's still unconscious.

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:32.900
<i>I see.</i>

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:37.450
According to the doctor, however,
he has no major external injuries.

00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:40.670
A thorough examination showed
nothing out of the ordinary, either.

00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:43.720
He should regain consciousness
at any moment.

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:49.360
Thank goodness.

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:50.630
Kaito...

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:12.920
Kimi no nounai e to shinnyuu
Gonna infiltrate your brain

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:15.670
Nemutteru suki ni baby, open the gate
While you're sleeping, baby, open the gate

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:17.510
Fukuzatsusugi security
Too-complicated security

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:20.260
Kakusareru to abakitakunaru
When something's hidden, it makes me want to expose it

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:24.770
Barabara ni chirabatte iru password o hiroiatsume
I'll gather up those loose, scattered passwords

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:29.480
Kakushin ni sematte yuku, sono shoutai o misete
And approach the core, so show me that true form

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:31.690
Kantan ni clear dekinai
I can't clear it easily

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:34.360
Saki nante motto yomenai
Can read what lies ahead even less

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.360
Kaidoku fukanou smile
A smile that can't be deciphered

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:38.660
Kiken na puzzle
A dangerous puzzle

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:40.570
Lock sareteta door aru nara
If there's a door that's been locked

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:43.410
Zutto tataite miru beki, kaza-ana hiraku wa
You must keep striking it, a crack will open

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:47.920
Eien ni hodokenai nazo nanka wa nai
No mystery remains unsolved forever

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:50.210
Makiokosu, it's a supernova!
It's forming, it's a supernova!

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:54.880
Tobikiri shigekiteki na hirameki o agemashou
I will give you thoroughly stimulating insight

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:57.130
Misskey-misskey la-tu-ma

00:01:57.130 --> 00:01:59.470
Yume no naka, it's a supernova!
In the middle of a dream, it's a supernova!

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:02.100
Watashi wa, sou, brain diver
I am, yes, a brain diver

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:07.980
Kimi ga sagashimotometeru kotae ni nareru made
Until I become familiar with the answer you seek

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:13.650
Brain diver

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:18.450
Brain diver

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:27.040
The Right of Friendship

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:29.180
Jeez!

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:32.100
I knew Kaito was an idiot, but...

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:33.870
No matter how much of a
friend this other guy was,

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:35.250
who goes running off

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:38.340
with the POG, let alone
one of their top brass?!

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:40.390
Kaito didn't know that.

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:42.290
That's why I'm callin' him an idiot.

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:47.730
I, Ana, think that you really like Kaito.

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:50.020
Huh?! Why would I?

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:51.330
I think so, too.

00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:52.600
Who asked you?!

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:54.610
Kaito's an idiot!

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:57.690
He left me to go running off to England.

00:02:57.690 --> 00:02:59.360
With a guy like that!

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:01.490
H..Hey!

00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:03.450
Cube!

00:03:06.270 --> 00:03:07.580
Dammit!

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:09.440
What's with this Puzzle of Fools?

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:11.570
Or this "Phi-Brain children" stuff?

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:14.290
It sounds like a bunch of nonsense.

00:03:14.910 --> 00:03:16.230
It's all BS!

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:21.220
<i>So, sure enough, he...</i>

00:03:21.580 --> 00:03:25.120
Yes, at the hands of Director Crossfield.

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:26.630
What shall we do?

00:03:26.630 --> 00:03:29.620
<i>Crossfield has carte
blanche within the POG.</i>

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:32.490
<i>Put simply, he is the
count's right-hand man.</i>

00:03:32.490 --> 00:03:34.840
<i>Please reign in his more
excessive behavior.</i>

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:36.470
Understood.

00:03:36.470 --> 00:03:37.530
<i>Very well.</i>

00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:43.530
No matter how you look at it,

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:45.570
having a comrade taken
out like this is just...

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:48.580
It's all a bit disagreeable.

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:54.380
I'll have to show him once and for all...

00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:58.430
Who's more suited to
be with Kaito, that is.

00:03:58.810 --> 00:04:01.050
Just wait, Rook Banjo Crossfield!

00:04:02.890 --> 00:04:05.900
Huh? Where am I?

00:04:14.360 --> 00:04:15.810
Is that...

00:04:25.630 --> 00:04:27.070
It's Morse Code!

00:04:27.940 --> 00:04:31.550
"Go there. Edison."

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:33.720
It's calling me!

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:36.330
Perfect timing.

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:39.210
I was just thinking
about where I could go

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:40.940
to strike down Kaito's enemy.

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:46.000
"Going forward, Kaito Daimon will walk

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:47.850
a path that runs alongside death.

00:04:48.570 --> 00:04:50.210
"If you accompany him,

00:04:50.210 --> 00:04:52.850
a road of hardship shall await you.

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:55.710
"If you are determined to go,

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:57.620
you must challenge the puzzle

00:04:57.620 --> 00:04:59.540
that Rook Banjo Crossfield has made.

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:01.590
"You must show your resolve.

00:05:01.590 --> 00:05:04.960
For that is proof of a fool
who does not fear death."

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:08.780
This, as instructed,

00:05:08.780 --> 00:05:11.370
was the message
transmitted to Cubik Galoit.

00:05:12.190 --> 00:05:13.120
Well done.

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:16.150
The plan is proceeding as you foresaw,

00:05:16.150 --> 00:05:18.150
and with no hiccups.

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:20.200
So why...

00:05:20.700 --> 00:05:23.660
They cling to Kaito like a mold.

00:05:23.660 --> 00:05:27.380
If we scrape them off,
Kaito is sure to turn more serious.

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:29.050
Isn't that right?

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:40.610
When he talks about him,

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:43.980
Kaito has a faraway, very
affectionate look in his eyes.

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:47.990
It's a look he's definitely
never given me.

00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:52.120
Sometimes I've wondered to myself.

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:54.050
Maybe Kaito's "clock"
stopped in the past,

00:05:54.050 --> 00:05:57.960
back when he was spending time with him.

00:05:58.230 --> 00:06:00.560
When I saw how Kaito
looked seeing him again

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:02.840
at Root Gakuen, that smile so big...

00:06:03.970 --> 00:06:06.220
I thought, "Sure enough!"

00:06:09.610 --> 00:06:12.820
Say, Ana, I don't get it.

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:15.350
Why would Rook do that to Kaito?

00:06:15.610 --> 00:06:18.750
I mean, Kaito definitely wouldn't think

00:06:18.750 --> 00:06:21.120
some bad guy was a friend.

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:24.780
Any friend of Kaito's
has to be a good guy!

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:27.160
I, Ana, think so too.

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:28.360
Then why?!

00:06:32.060 --> 00:06:33.530
I, Ana, think so too.

00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:35.350
I told you already.

00:06:35.350 --> 00:06:36.970
Kaito's an idiot.

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:39.330
Any friend of an idiot...

00:06:40.050 --> 00:06:41.830
is gonna be an idiot.

00:06:44.620 --> 00:06:47.530
An abandoned military base?

00:06:49.540 --> 00:06:51.650
I'm here, just like you wanted!

00:06:51.650 --> 00:06:52.850
POG!

00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:41.680
Is no one here?

00:07:41.680 --> 00:07:45.120
You call a genius like me out here
and then keep me waiting?

00:07:46.540 --> 00:07:48.810
Or have you gotten scared?

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:58.030
You were informed that death awaited you,

00:07:58.030 --> 00:08:00.160
yet it seems you've come
here rather than escaping.

00:08:02.810 --> 00:08:06.040
Normally, this would be worthy of praise,

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:09.780
but in this instance, the
only word that befits you is:

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:11.050
"Imbecile."

00:08:11.530 --> 00:08:13.240
Who are you, old man?

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:15.930
I'm here to challenge Rook.

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:18.580
He's the one who's been
cruel to Kaito, right?

00:08:18.580 --> 00:08:19.930
Go get him!

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:21.020
You jest.

00:08:21.260 --> 00:08:23.460
There would be no reason for Master Rook

00:08:23.460 --> 00:08:26.030
to make an appearance
for one such as you.

00:08:26.030 --> 00:08:28.590
I've come here to get
vengeance for Kaito.

00:08:28.590 --> 00:08:30.570
Just hurry up and call him.

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:31.570
Silence!

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:36.730
Seeking to defy Master Rook is
the epitome of foolishness.

00:08:36.730 --> 00:08:39.080
I'm Kaito's friend.

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:40.950
It's only natural that
I'd seek vengeance!

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:42.540
Friend?

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:44.930
You think you have the right to call

00:08:44.930 --> 00:08:47.580
yourself a friend of Kaito Daimon?

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:50.320
You were called here today

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:52.860
because there is something
I wish to tell you.

00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:55.980
Will you return and tell
it to your companions?

00:08:57.210 --> 00:08:59.790
"You are all hindrances
preventing Kaito Daimon

00:08:59.790 --> 00:09:02.680
from reaching his full potential,

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:05.100
"so please remove yourselves
from his presence."

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:07.680
You sure are funny, old man.

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:09.550
I'm a genius!

00:09:09.550 --> 00:09:12.600
So, of course I'm suitable
as Kaito's friend, right?

00:09:13.790 --> 00:09:15.930
It seems it can't be helped.

00:09:15.930 --> 00:09:18.490
Very well: I would have
you show me proof.

00:09:36.350 --> 00:09:37.340
What is this?

00:09:38.370 --> 00:09:42.560
It is a puzzle that Master
Rook has prepared for you.

00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:45.620
I shall now explain the rules.

00:09:45.940 --> 00:09:48.860
Please solve the puzzles in order,
as monitors one

00:09:48.860 --> 00:09:50.560
through five turn on.

00:09:51.430 --> 00:09:54.070
Before each counter reaches zero,

00:09:54.800 --> 00:09:57.840
you must enter values so
that all numbers surrounding

00:09:57.840 --> 00:10:00.440
each puzzle become 10.

00:10:01.010 --> 00:10:04.710
You cannot enter the same number
twice on a single row.

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:11.070
Only parts of the numbers are displayed.

00:10:11.070 --> 00:10:12.630
So that's a hint?

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:14.090
Exactly.

00:10:16.880 --> 00:10:18.500
This one first?

00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:24.970
It seems you're in a hurry to die.

00:10:26.750 --> 00:10:28.280
Very well, let's begin.

00:10:28.920 --> 00:10:32.310
The imbecile begins on
his path to destruction.

00:10:35.510 --> 00:10:38.090
<i>If each side equals 10,</i>

00:10:38.090 --> 00:10:42.740
<i>then this side can only
be 2 x 5 or 5 x 2.</i>

00:10:43.290 --> 00:10:45.240
<i>If 5 were to go here,</i>

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:47.300
<i>then only 2 could follow.</i>

00:10:48.170 --> 00:10:51.450
<i>If I entered 1, then 5 would be last,</i>

00:10:51.450 --> 00:10:53.440
<i>and the same number would appear twice</i>

00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:55.210
<i>
on that side, making it invalid.</i>

00:10:55.510 --> 00:10:58.410
<i>Therefore, the numbers that go here</i>

00:10:58.410 --> 00:11:00.260
<i>
have to be 2 and 5.</i>

00:11:01.030 --> 00:11:04.010
<i>A simple matter of trial
and error, isn't it?</i>

00:11:06.290 --> 00:11:07.900
<i>This will be easy.</i>

00:11:18.070 --> 00:11:18.960
Kaito?

00:11:26.070 --> 00:11:29.460
Nonoha, Gammon, Ana...

00:11:30.140 --> 00:11:31.040
Why...

00:11:30.140 --> 00:11:31.880
Kaito!

00:11:31.880 --> 00:11:34.040
Kaito, Kaito, Kaito!

00:11:34.040 --> 00:11:35.710
It hurts! It hurts! It hurts, Nonoha!

00:11:35.710 --> 00:11:37.000
Sorry.

00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:39.350
Thank goodness.

00:12:00.940 --> 00:12:01.990
Rook!

00:12:04.440 --> 00:12:05.370
Kaito!

00:12:06.520 --> 00:12:07.620
Where you goin'?!

00:12:08.710 --> 00:12:10.100
Move it, Gammon.

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:13.130
I got something I gotta make sure...

00:12:11.650 --> 00:12:13.130
Open yer eyes!

00:12:13.130 --> 00:12:15.180
You almost got killed!

00:12:15.180 --> 00:12:16.250
Shut up!

00:12:16.510 --> 00:12:18.380
Wake up, dammit!

00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:23.130
I'm in a hella crappy mood right now!

00:12:32.950 --> 00:12:34.140
Dumbass.

00:12:52.150 --> 00:12:55.150
There's no way I can't solve this puzzle.

00:12:55.760 --> 00:12:57.840
After all, I'm a genius.

00:12:58.170 --> 00:13:01.710
I'm much smarter than Rook,
the guy who made this!

00:13:07.560 --> 00:13:08.550
Oh, no!

00:13:12.800 --> 00:13:15.920
What's this? Not all you claim to be, eh?

00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:17.850
No! I didn't make a mistake!

00:13:17.850 --> 00:13:19.220
My hand slipped!

00:13:44.350 --> 00:13:45.960
Please rest easy.

00:13:45.960 --> 00:13:48.820
Your death approaches by degrees.

00:13:50.070 --> 00:13:52.960
Only when you've failed the final puzzle

00:13:53.080 --> 00:13:56.770
will the shell strike this hangar.

00:13:58.060 --> 00:14:02.290
Please, you can't go
getting scared already.

00:14:03.460 --> 00:14:05.730
The countdown at the No. 2 computer

00:14:05.730 --> 00:14:07.780
has already started.

00:14:19.790 --> 00:14:23.770
Oh, yes, I forgot to tell you
something very important:

00:14:23.770 --> 00:14:26.680
there is a way that you can live even if

00:14:26.680 --> 00:14:29.050
you don't solve the puzzle.

00:14:29.050 --> 00:14:31.290
It's quite easy.

00:14:31.290 --> 00:14:34.430
You simply flee from the puzzle.

00:14:56.820 --> 00:15:00.150
Oh, that must have been rough, Kaito.

00:15:14.870 --> 00:15:16.730
Do you want to be alone?

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:23.870
Let's go, Gammon.

00:15:23.870 --> 00:15:24.730
Huh?

00:15:25.200 --> 00:15:26.360
Yeah.

00:15:54.430 --> 00:15:57.000
Well, with Kaito bein' all like he is,

00:15:57.000 --> 00:15:59.140
there's no reason for you to be...

00:15:59.140 --> 00:16:01.350
Let's hold a party to cheer up Kaito!

00:16:03.530 --> 00:16:06.170
Uh, I don't think he's in the mood for...

00:16:06.170 --> 00:16:08.550
I, Ana, agree!

00:16:09.040 --> 00:16:10.250
You really shouldn't.

00:16:10.250 --> 00:16:11.860
Majority rules.

00:16:12.390 --> 00:16:14.280
All students of Root Gakuen who think

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:16.060
having it is a good idea:

00:16:16.060 --> 00:16:18.490
Yes, yes, yes, yes, yes!

00:16:16.980 --> 00:16:18.490
Hey, now.

00:16:39.470 --> 00:16:41.730
This is getting harder and harder.

00:16:42.160 --> 00:16:43.700
Ironic, isn't it?

00:16:43.700 --> 00:16:46.730
For numbers to give me this much trouble?

00:16:47.170 --> 00:16:50.030
I know because numbers
is what I'm good at.

00:16:50.030 --> 00:16:51.980
But whether I can solve this last

00:16:51.980 --> 00:16:54.910
problem within the time limit is 50-50!

00:16:55.410 --> 00:16:58.550
Wouldn't it be better if you just ran?

00:16:58.550 --> 00:17:01.160
Behold, you are close to death.

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:16.430
Now then, it's about time
that I had you leave.

00:17:16.690 --> 00:17:19.500
I don't much fancy
entertaining an imbecile

00:17:19.500 --> 00:17:21.630
any more than this.

00:17:32.550 --> 00:17:35.490
Should I just throw it all away and run?

00:17:35.490 --> 00:17:38.290
Or should I not give
up and keep fighting?

00:17:38.290 --> 00:17:39.430
What should I do?

00:17:39.430 --> 00:17:40.370
What should I do?!

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:43.330
The answer's obvious!

00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:44.120
If I were Kaito...

00:17:46.490 --> 00:17:48.790
If I were Kaito, I wouldn't hesitate!

00:18:07.680 --> 00:18:10.030
If not trying is worth regretting,

00:18:10.030 --> 00:18:11.940
I'll try and regret later!

00:18:32.450 --> 00:18:36.060
No, ain't never considered losing.

00:18:36.060 --> 00:18:38.370
Goin' forward, obstinately,

00:18:38.370 --> 00:18:40.310
bein' a little shy because of it...

00:18:40.310 --> 00:18:42.890
That's the Kaito that I'm crazy about!

00:18:43.280 --> 00:18:44.010
I...

00:18:44.380 --> 00:18:47.020
I want to be like Kaito!

00:19:32.120 --> 00:19:33.690
Excellently done.

00:19:37.830 --> 00:19:40.380
I beat him - Rook.

00:19:40.380 --> 00:19:41.240
Yes.

00:19:42.060 --> 00:19:44.660
He was still young at this point.

00:19:45.380 --> 00:19:48.920
Master Rook made this puzzle

00:19:48.920 --> 00:19:51.920
just about the time that you were born.

00:19:51.920 --> 00:19:52.880
When he was five.

00:19:53.650 --> 00:19:56.690
Five?! He made this at that age?

00:19:56.690 --> 00:20:00.540
Do you not think that someone
possessing such capabilities

00:20:00.540 --> 00:20:04.380
is more suited to be
Kaito Daimon's companion?

00:20:04.380 --> 00:20:06.390
Well, "genius"?

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:35.390
Union Jack's apple juice sure is sour.

00:20:37.830 --> 00:20:39.370
Now then,

00:20:39.370 --> 00:20:43.170
what can one not born as

00:20:43.170 --> 00:20:45.430
a Phi-Brain child, like me, do?

00:20:46.330 --> 00:20:49.210
Thus, I think "puzzles" and "nozzles"

00:20:49.210 --> 00:20:52.060
must surely be related, right?

00:20:52.060 --> 00:20:55.880
I, Ana, would rather be nuzzling.

00:20:55.880 --> 00:20:58.940
Thank you, much obliged!

00:21:03.750 --> 00:21:06.060
Speaking of Genius Terrace...

00:21:06.060 --> 00:21:07.580
Speaking of!

00:21:07.580 --> 00:21:09.790
What does it have in common with
Puzzle Club members?

00:21:09.790 --> 00:21:11.380
What is it?

00:21:11.380 --> 00:21:14.550
I, Ana, think they're both
like prickly blooms that

00:21:14.550 --> 00:21:17.350
sprout up in the midnight sun of the desert.

00:21:17.350 --> 00:21:18.560
Well said!

00:21:18.560 --> 00:21:20.980
Wait, I don't really get that...

00:21:20.980 --> 00:21:22.650
But in any case, that's
just like you, Ana!

00:21:36.330 --> 00:21:37.230
Kaito!

00:21:38.510 --> 00:21:40.950
We're doing a Cheer Kaito Up Party now!

00:21:40.950 --> 00:21:42.640
You do it too, Cube!

00:21:43.370 --> 00:21:46.000
You're his friend too, right? Please!

00:21:53.960 --> 00:21:57.680
Sorry, I'm feeling thirsty.

00:21:57.680 --> 00:21:59.100
I'm gonna buy something to drink.

00:21:59.100 --> 00:22:01.180
Hey, don't run off!

00:22:01.180 --> 00:22:03.270
I'll get some for everyone.

00:22:06.130 --> 00:22:07.400
What's with him?

00:22:08.000 --> 00:22:09.970
Well, you can't put someone on the spot

00:22:09.970 --> 00:22:11.970
like that and expect 'em to deliver.

00:22:12.350 --> 00:22:14.010
Then you do it, Gammon.

00:22:14.010 --> 00:22:15.020
Huh?!

00:22:15.340 --> 00:22:17.930
It's been just me and Ana so far!

00:22:17.930 --> 00:22:19.520
You do something too!

00:22:19.520 --> 00:22:21.020
Uh, well, in that case...

00:22:21.330 --> 00:22:23.890
Speakin' of old friends...

00:22:24.530 --> 00:22:26.980
What the hell kind of joke is that?

00:22:26.980 --> 00:22:28.880
What the hell are you doin' to me?!

00:22:37.240 --> 00:22:41.540
Tsukue no ue de umareta sekai
A world born on top of a desk

00:22:41.540 --> 00:22:47.340
Ichiban saki ni kimi ni misetakatta
I wanted to show it to you first of all

00:22:47.770 --> 00:22:52.090
Karappo no heya sotto nukedashite
I sneaked silently out of that empty room

00:22:52.090 --> 00:22:57.210
Hashirihajimeteta
And started running

00:22:58.290 --> 00:23:02.610
Iki hazumasete oka o noboru to
Breathing heavily, I climbed the hill

00:23:02.610 --> 00:23:08.220
Kimi ga saki ni tsuite matte ita ne
And you were already there, waiting

00:23:08.900 --> 00:23:13.160
Takusan no hajimete kimi to mitsuketa
There were so many treasures that I first

00:23:13.160 --> 00:23:17.910
Takaramono datta
Discovered with you

00:23:18.410 --> 00:23:24.020
Kanashisa de afureta toki wa
That time when I was overcome with sadness

00:23:24.020 --> 00:23:26.600
Nanimo iwazu ni tada
You said nothing

00:23:26.600 --> 00:23:29.250
Soba ni ite kureta ne
Just stayed there by my side, didn't you?

00:23:29.250 --> 00:23:33.910
Imademo wasurenai yo
Even now, I haven't forgotten

00:23:33.910 --> 00:23:39.180
Mata aou ne, yakusoku o shiyou
Let's meet again, let's make it a promise

00:23:39.180 --> 00:23:44.400
Kei wa shinai, ano hi no sayonara
It won't fade, the "goodbye" of that day

00:23:44.400 --> 00:23:50.050
Boku no subete, kimi ga kureta michi
Everything I have, the path you gave me

00:23:50.050 --> 00:23:58.960
Zutto kokoro no naka hikaru yo
Will always shine within my heart

00:24:03.050 --> 00:24:05.500
You've done well, Da Vinci.

00:24:05.500 --> 00:24:06.290
Huh?

00:24:06.290 --> 00:24:07.840
I am Maze.

00:24:07.840 --> 00:24:10.120
This is the puzzle you
shall soon attempt.

00:24:10.120 --> 00:24:11.720
It's calling me.

00:24:11.720 --> 00:24:12.640
I think it's this one.

00:24:12.640 --> 00:24:14.810
What? Hey, wait!

00:24:14.810 --> 00:24:15.980
No, it's this way!

00:24:15.980 --> 00:24:18.170
Just where do you think you're going?!

00:24:18.170 --> 00:24:20.850
I, Ana, am hungry...

00:24:20.760 --> 00:24:24.680
Next time, "Blue Sun, Red Moon"

00:24:22.250 --> 00:24:27.150
Blue Sun, Red Moon

00:24:24.680 --> 00:24:27.650
You're doing this on
purpose, aren't you?!
